From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 02:34:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 127/128] dynarmic A64: sign-extending loads in one instruction
 (LDRSB, LDRSH, LDRSW with fastmem)

A plain load whose one use sign-extends it is a movsx/movsxd from memory (to 32 bits with the
register's upper half zeroed, or 64), the extension nothing, instead of a load and a movsx/movsxd
after it. Fastmem sites only (PeepholeQuad marks them); their fallbacks are stubs that sign-extend
the callback's value; a range-check miss takes the fallback. game.c for AArch64: -1.0%.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
